  "question": {
    "text": "The volume of an ideal gas $(\\gamma=1.5)$ is changed adiabatically from 5 litres to 4 litres. The ratio of initial pressure to final pressure is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "hCT5K",
      "text": "$\\frac{16}{25}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "k4wV1",
      "text": "$\\frac{4}{5}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "foOrr",
      "text": "$\\frac{8}{5 \\sqrt{5}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "Ctjh7",
      "text": "$\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For Adiabatic process\n$\\begin{aligned} & P_i V_i=P_f V_f^\\gamma \\\\ & P_i(5)^{1.5}=P_f(4)^{1.5} \\\\ & \\frac{P_i}{P_f}=\\left(\\frac{4}{5}\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}=\\frac{4}{5} \\cdot\\left(\\frac{4}{5}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\Rightarrow \\frac{8}{5 \\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
